// H-MEASURE M7-A (G2-09): does TradingView check a LEVERAGED opening on its entry bar?
// One long market entry, placed on the signal bar 2025-11-21 07:15 UTC, fills at the open of
// 2025-11-21 07:30 UTC, whose low sits far under that open. margin_long=5 (the Pine percent),
// quantity = 16 x equity / signal close: the entry bar's low breaches the requirement.
// Timeout close 3 bars after the entry bar.
//@version=6
strategy("hm-m7a-eth-m5-k16-1121", overlay=true, initial_capital=1000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1, pyramiding=1,
     margin_long=5, margin_short=5, commission_value=0, slippage=0,
     process_orders_on_close=false)
if time == timestamp("UTC", 2025, 11, 21, 7, 15) and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = math.floor(16 * strategy.equity / close * 1000) / 1000)
if strategy.position_size > 0 and bar_index - strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(0) >= 3
    strategy.close("L", comment="timeout")
